# Flow — What's New / post-install self-check, driven against the PC (h5) client.
#
# Why the h5 client and not the RN app: the RN bundle has no react-native-web
# build, so `agent-device --platform web` cannot open it. The What's New screen
# is deliberately mirrored by clients/h5/src/screens/WhatsNewScreen.tsx, which
# IS a browser app — and this replay is its behavioural proof. The RN screen's
# presence + wiring is pinned separately in scripts/e2e-local.sh (assertion
# `expo-whats-new`), same split the workspace tabs already use.
#
# What it proves end to end: the What's New page renders for the shipped
# version, "我知道了" lands on the 工坊 (ChatHome) page, and the workspace modal
# opens with all four tabs. This is the install loop from the boss's seat.
#
# Owned by scripts/e2e-local.sh, which supplies ${E2E_H5_URL} via --env and
# starts the h5 dev server before this runs.

open ${E2E_H5_URL}/#/whats-new
wait text "What's New" 60000
find text "ChatHome" exists
screenshot clients/expo/replays/evidence/whats-new-01-screen.png
click label="我知道了"
wait text "工作空间" 60000
click label="工作空间"
wait text "对话" 60000
find text "预览" exists
find text "文件" exists
find text "终端" exists
screenshot clients/expo/replays/evidence/whats-new-02-workspace.png
